+# T1_F252 — Standing-red paydown (154 ids, 13 classes)
+**Tier 1 · Registered work item (operator ruling A, 2026-07-28) ·
+Executes before F050 · Depends on: the F251 baseline · Blocks/used
+by: gate honesty, the F075 baseline**
+
+## Goal & Done
+The 154 deterministic standing-red test ids catalogued by F251 reach
+an explicit terminal state, class by class: root-cause fix, honest
+test update, or an operator-decided retirement — never a silent skip.
+DONE when three consecutive full-suite runs (pytest -n auto -q)
+produce identical failure sets and that set is empty except for
+explicitly quarantined tests, with F251's quarantine rules unchanged
+(marker/skip + reason string + backlog reference per test; never
+deletion, never blanket directory skips, never weakened assertions).
+
+## Work breakdown
+Canonical id list: .agent/f251_baseline/class_map.txt (F251 branch,
+merged history). Priority order per the ruling: product-bug classes
+first, then product change, then test rewrites, then doc/text drift,
+then operator-decision classes.
+1. Product bugs: D8 flight-plan schema_v regression (3) · D10
+   discover-commands CLI rc=1 / non-JSON (8) · D11 malformed TOML
+   raises BudgetConfigError not FenceConfigError (3).
+2. Product change: D5 CLI requires a registered project, cwd
+   coupling (11) · D7 dev_server private names removed (6) · D9
+   command-catalog classification drift (3) · D13 review-zip /
+   evidence packaging drift (11).
+3. Test rewrites: D6 incomplete MagicMock vs real comparison (9).
+4. Doc/text drift: D1 doc/file missing at pre-restructure flat path
+   (36) · D14 misc drift, uncategorised (46). Note: the ruling
+   mentioned a "D2"; no such class exists in the catalog — the
+   catalog is authoritative.
+5. Operator-decision classes — each carries a per-class decision
+   request for its round: D3 apps/ui legacy/*.tsx absent (10) — fix
+   the tests now or park them until the Tier 5 UI build? · D12
+   .claude/agents/remedy-reviewer.md absent (1) — restore the file
+   or retire the test?
+6. The two stopped F-A ids from F251: the real-Vite probe binds the
+   product's apps/ui port; the supervisor teardown guard's fix
+   reaches the product stop/ownership path. Both need product
+   change.
+7. D4 design decision (9 ids): the .agent contract tests read LIVE
+   state files, so every round's bookkeeping moves them (proven in
+   F251 R2: two ids flipped after a live_review rewrite). Explicit
+   item: rebuild fixture-based vs keep live-coupled with the
+   movement documented.
+
+## Rules
+Per-class rounds, normal review discipline. F251's quarantine rules
+apply unchanged inside F252. A class whose fix exceeds its stated
+bucket stops and reports — never silent scope drift. Every class
+round ends by recording the full-suite delta (which ids left the
+standing set).
+
+## Out of scope
+New features beyond what a class fix strictly requires; UI build-out
+(D3 is a decision request, not an implementation order).
+
+## Orchestrator brief
+One class per round where possible; the product-bug classes are
+ordinary bug fixes with tests. The ledger pin
+(tests/docs/test_docs_consistency.py) moves atomically with any
+feature-file or STATUS change, always.
